  o A dump shows its seed as a hidden one's digest ("hidden#..."), and a
    game's feed shows a player's own seed as given: a dump and a game are
    paired by their levels' layout hashes, not by the seed shown.

  o Secrecy: the full dump is the whole dungeon, as secret as the seed
    until the race is over (A3). A layout hash on its own tells nothing
    about its level: it is salted from the end of the seed's chain, so it
    can't be looked up in tables made from other seeds nor traced back to
    the seed; consumers match hashes, never recompute them.


